            <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-white ring-1 ring-indigo-200">
              <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-indigo-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 4.5v15m7.5-7.5h-15" /></svg>
            </span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900">Or build your own</h3>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Every other gauge under Broker health opens a monitor too, without a starting threshold. Build one by hand on any metric that names a queue, or group it by the attribute that names the queue so that every queue of a system alerts on its own.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <a href="/docs/telemetry/queues#alerting" class="mt-4 lg:mt-0 inline-flex flex-shrink-0 items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-700">Read about queue alerts <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5L21 12m0 0l-7.5 7.5" /></svg></a>
