        <!-- Section header -->
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-indigo-50 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-indigo-700 ring-1 ring-inset ring-indigo-600/20 mb-6">
            <svg class="h-4 w-4 text-indigo-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
            </svg>
            <span class="text-sm font-medium text-indigo-700">Advanced capabilities</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-4xl text-balance">
            Built for the way messaging actually runs
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600">
            Reply queues, retries, five naming generations and cloud metrics that arrive late: the list stays one row per real queue.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Feature cards grid -->
        <div class="mx-auto mt-16 max-w-7xl">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">

            <!-- Card 1: No queue per request -->
            <div class="group relative">
              <div class="relative h-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8 transition-all duration-300 hover:border-indigo-200 hover:shadow-lg">
                <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 ring-1 ring-indigo-200">
                  <svg class="h-6 w-6 text-indigo-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 3c2.755 0 5.455.232 8.083.678.533.09.917.556.917 1.096v1.044a2.25 2.25 0 01-.659 1.591l-5.432 5.432a2.25 2.25 0 00-.659 1.591v2.927a2.25 2.25 0 01-1.244 2.013L9.75 21v-6.568a2.25 2.25 0 00-.659-1.591L3.659 7.409A2.25 2.25 0 013 5.818V4.774c0-.54.384-1.006.917-1.096A48.32 48.32 0 0112 3z" />
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">No Queue per Request</h3>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Temporary and anonymous destinations, server-named reply queues such as RabbitMQ's <code class="text-sm bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">amq.gen-…</code>, NATS inboxes and the placeholders instrumentations report instead of a name never become queues. A UUID inside a name becomes <code class="text-sm bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">{uuid}</code>, so a reply queue per request is one queue.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Card 2: JMS and ActiveMQ -->
            <div class="group relative">
              <div class="relative h-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8 transition-all duration-300 hover:border-blue-200 hover:shadow-lg">
                <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-blue-50 ring-1 ring-blue-200">
                  <svg class="h-6 w-6 text-blue-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13.19 8.688a4.5 4.5 0 011.242 7.244l-4.5 4.5a4.5 4.5 0 01-6.364-6.364l1.757-1.757m13.35-.622l1.757-1.757a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364-6.364l-4.5 4.5a4.5 4.5 0 001.242 7.244" />
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">JMS and ActiveMQ, One Queue</h3>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Java applications reach ActiveMQ through the JMS API, whose spans say <code class="text-sm bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">jms</code> whatever the broker, while the broker's own metrics can only say <code class="text-sm bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">activemq</code>. Both land on one queue: it shows as JMS until the broker's metrics arrive, and as Apache ActiveMQ from then on.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Card 3: Lifecycle -->
            <div class="group relative">
              <div class="relative h-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8 transition-all duration-300 hover:border-amber-200 hover:shadow-lg">
                <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-amber-50 ring-1 ring-amber-200">
                  <svg class="h-6 w-6 text-amber-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M20.25 7.5l-.625 10.632a2.25 2.25 0 01-2.247 2.118H6.622a2.25 2.25 0 01-2.247-2.118L3.75 7.5m8.25 3v6.75m0 0l-3-3m3 3l3-3M3.375 7.5h17.25c.621 0 1.125-.504 1.125-1.125v-1.5c0-.621-.504-1.125-1.125-1.125H3.375c-.621 0-1.125.504-1.125 1.125v1.5c0 .621.504 1.125 1.125 1.125z" />
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">A List That Cleans Up</h3>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">A discovered queue nobody has seen for 7 days is archived on its own, unless somebody renamed it, described it, labelled it or gave it owners, and it comes back by itself when it is seen again. Archive one yourself to dismiss it for good.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Card 4: Owners & labels -->
            <div class="group relative">
              <div class="relative h-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8 transition-all duration-300 hover:border-indigo-200 hover:shadow-lg">
                <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-indigo-50 ring-1 ring-indigo-200">
                  <svg class="h-6 w-6 text-indigo-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M18 18.72a9.094 9.094 0 003.741-.479 3 3 0 00-4.682-2.72m.94 3.198l.001.031c0 .225-.012.447-.037.666A11.944 11.944 0 0112 21c-2.17 0-4.207-.576-5.963-1.584A6.062 6.062 0 016 18.719m12 0a5.971 5.971 0 00-.941-3.197m0 0A5.995 5.995 0 0012 12.75a5.995 5.995 0 00-5.058 2.772m0 0a3 3 0 00-4.681 2.72 8.986 8.986 0 003.74.477m.94-3.197a5.971 5.971 0 00-.94 3.197M15 6.75a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0zm6 3a2.25 2.25 0 11-4.5 0 2.25 2.25 0 014.5 0zm-13.5 0a2.25 2.25 0 11-4.5 0 2.25 2.25 0 014.5 0z" />
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Owners, Labels &amp; Rules</h3>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Give every queue owning teams and users, label it, and let label and owner rules pick queues up by name, description, labels or messaging system: a system pattern of <code class="text-sm bg-gray-100 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">kafka</code> matches every Kafka topic.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Card 5: Late cloud metrics -->
            <div class="group relative">
              <div class="relative h-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8 transition-all duration-300 hover:border-sky-200 hover:shadow-lg">
                <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-sky-50 ring-1 ring-sky-200">
                  <svg class="h-6 w-6 text-sky-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M2.25 15a4.5 4.5 0 004.5 4.5H18a3.75 3.75 0 001.332-7.257 3 3 0 00-3.758-3.848 5.25 5.25 0 00-10.233 2.33A4.502 4.502 0 002.25 15z" />
                  </svg>
                </div>
                <h3 class="mt-6 text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Late Cloud Metrics, Handled</h3>
                <p class="mt-4 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">CloudWatch, Azure Monitor and Cloud Monitoring publish each number minutes after the time it measures. Discovery reads their metrics from the last hour, so a late point still finds its queue, and monitors built from SQS, SNS and Pub/Sub charts start with windows long enough to hold one.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Card 6: Traces -->
            <div class="group relative">
              <a href="/product/traces" class="block relative h-full rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8 transition-all duration-300 hover:border-yellow-200 hover:shadow-lg">
