            Pay for data, or run it yourself
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">OneUptime Cloud</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Usage-based: $0.10 per GB of telemetry ingested. There is no fee per queue, topic, partition or broker, so a new topic or another consumer group costs what its spans and metrics weigh.</p>
            <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="h-4 w-4 text-indigo-500 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>No per-queue or per-broker licence</li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="h-4 w-4 text-indigo-500 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>Discovery reads the telemetry you already send</li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="h-4 w-4 text-indigo-500 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>On-call, status pages, and incidents included</li>
            </ul>
            <a href="/pricing" class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium text-indigo-600 hover:text-indigo-700">See pricing <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5L21 12m0 0l-7.5 7.5" /></svg></a>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-8">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Self-Hosted</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Queues is part of the open source Community Edition (Apache 2.0). Run it on your own Kubernetes cluster or Docker host, keep every span and broker metric inside your network, and point your collectors at your own instance instead of ours. Everything else is identical.</p>
            <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="h-4 w-4 text-indigo-500 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>Air-gapped and data-residency deployments supported</li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="h-4 w-4 text-indigo-500 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>Discovery threshold, auto-create budget and archive window are tunable</li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="h-4 w-4 text-indigo-500 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" /></svg>Same collector configs, same pages, same thresholds</li>
